b/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438194} {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438195} :answer-field/id #uuid "4056b817-e800-5678-8e9e-22469e604236" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "544516cf-cdec-5de8-af07-1ff7e5be101e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36004" :question/problem "![](images/15/1597ad53471d0d9b44812c5caa31bcb160cfa150d1df9a9314447fa49e62ccff.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-6,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-6,4)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [4,10)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-6,0]$ and $x\\in [4,10).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/7c/7cb282e3fa66af801ff03816973d5f5f1d0cb41e39d08a8addd27d7aa9c5b9df.png)\n\n      \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[-6,4]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/00/000953609a7b3e13ad09473ead62f96aa895c7f94aa618884e69883595004fd4.png)\n\n \n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6dd990f-2330-5d0c-81b4-6370f4d92329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438196} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438197} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa5f1a4-0dd6-545a-95f5-013d457374c6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f744e7a-172a-583f-b418-720dc54aa6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438198} {:answer/id #uuid "37107bf0-d7a1-5dde-a57d-5db8ff5c2424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f744e7a-172a-583f-b418-720dc54aa6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438198} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7ed940-ad9d-549b-8ff8-c6ed363707ab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65a72c59-feca-5579-98db-917865bf0995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438200} {:answer/id #uuid "73492b46-ebe8-5272-ad45-7118928025ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73492b46-ebe8-5272-ad45-7118928025ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438201} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7aa9bfc-97c1-53ea-b5a1-715f3992c90c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f06fc453-0309-58aa-ad2f-fecdd1ab38c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-36008" :question/problem "![](images/27/279c3cd6084423d913186f4ba467ea50d0f794cf54773785777cb8841f5c2ca1.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,-1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in [-1,3]$\n- **III.** $x\\in [0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-1]$ and on $x\\in [0,1].$  Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/03/0388335095ed530ce07d278f82be5eb3bff14859db64b6e9ec47da27861bb657.png)\n\n    \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval. $x\\in [-1,3]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/52/522b5661aaf9b7640c305b8cefd06f49cc8eed590f3ae736fc6720e6165bc3a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff35ccf9-01ac-52ac-880d-c4dc02e90a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438202} {:answer/id #uuid "94989d8f-895b-52e3-984a-8b2b79d456fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94989d8f-895b-52e3-984a-8b2b79d456fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438203} :answer-field/id #uuid "aacdaa79-2d58-50ce-8011-be966bc39789" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39cdea1e-5a53-54bf-bea0-69611a5b3d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438204} {:answer/id #uuid "92557738-afb1-50f3-81d0-90a570989d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39cdea1e-5a53-54bf-bea0-69611a5b3d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438204} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf49524-0b72-5fcd-b414-ca90461589ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8cc712-dfda-5034-8c6b-b4e359500cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438206} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ceb92f-1179-5f20-aac2-a8c21430d24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3ceb92f-1179-5f20-aac2-a8c21430d24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438207} :answer-field/id #uuid "496eb34a-e1a6-5d05-95ad-5faa3b236c5b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aef31e6b-2918-5842-b5c4-348781827064" :question/math-academy-id "q-36010" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-2|$ by $1$ unit up to get $f(x)=|x-2|+1.$\n\n![](images/ce/ceab1637313ae53869cc1e59f6a56ad6cb920a83dffba482558b696188df0d36.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (2,4].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a47169838785b6f4ac78253252bcedc3c2cb752a655feac9945e20dd40563b4f.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/14/14ed35294e1179ffd9efaf87fa8ac1eb99853a7da344e462c2cb0dda74c3b78f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88cfd433-113f-5181-b46c-34920cbe5bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438208} {:answer/id #uuid "92c8406c-f814-57d1-83d4-a13a818e5eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92c8406c-f814-57d1-83d4-a13a818e5eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0273b980-43eb-564c-872d-0589397d574e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890e79b7-dfdd-538c-8e9a-7abc3f553b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438210} {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438211} :answer-field/id #uuid "5568fe44-2db6-5364-963c-2b0dbd971f58" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438212} {:answer/id #uuid "cfff16d0-eaff-5775-853f-d6b2f96cf631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438212} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f018c0-f200-5146-8568-3810e8f2e7b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d31db013-e3f7-5fe2-aefa-8428da418673" :question/math-academy-id "q-36011" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b02c2e94e144935f0ff96846cd51b5a969fa8f884a7ca1d09abb231b7c945232.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-4,-2)$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-2,3]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-4,-2)$ and $x\\in [-2,3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/53/53fe88780b2ccb7522d2f1baa711162ec99300c2a2d4da29bba9ca532026cd07.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on  the interval $x\\in [-3,3]$  because some lines will  intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/63/63cee4fc05ab17a8e69d9bfae578fa83c24d73e4677065a54a33a25e0871e718.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ca90ac0-fdc1-56ec-bb51-072e1c20d1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438220} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ac5c50-b4c2-5723-a4c6-e5840e08cedd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ca90ac0-fdc1-56ec-bb51-072e1c20d1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438220} :answer-field/id #uuid "beadee01-3a5c-57eb-8fdd-3c86a4c03e46" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2308f466-35ae-5427-a685-1a00a0710d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438222} {:answer/id #uuid "0312f73e-27c1-5028-a6de-b70ef24c915a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0312f73e-27c1-5028-a6de-b70ef24c915a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438223} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f53a29c-1c33-59d0-a673-d3b51504ed3a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9b43604-8edf-57f2-b9de-096dcbcc5dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438224} {:answer/id #uuid "b28f36fb-3166-55fa-8439-85a4e2c30bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b43604-8edf-57f2-b9de-096dcbcc5dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438224} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c22e257-18b9-5973-9c9f-ae85ffec73b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aef7162-d0e5-5631-91ce-694e2ecc3ef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438226} {:answer/id #uuid "c1588c7f-143f-535f-b50f-e63a5091e059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aef7162-d0e5-5631-91ce-694e2ecc3ef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438226} :answer-field/id #uuid "56db77a8-773c-594c-afa2-0b04cacc3d8a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0429905-029f-5585-ac21-8d23fa4141fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-36063" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1dd593e8b48b13ec512a3e0c823ec0aaac4f5341bd519c7bb9b04648f95f4251.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/2a/2a68cbeceea9173ab7a53d334d073e9779b048ad8946fd3ff81b09adb79cee98.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graph II, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph II shows a one-to-one function. As a result, this function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, III and IV, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. These are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc69b98-00eb-5840-b90d-c96ba4931e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438228} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438229} :answer-field/id #uuid "559a6aac-97fe-50a0-8beb-d1323671d7f8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a97abe-d55d-5007-b4fd-6937cc34e17a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438230} {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438231} :answer-field/id #uuid "6639d61d-bf93-5072-838b-4370ba49c0ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438232} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf0f901-76be-5f84-b0ee-c5cd9c1a5306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438232} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f0537b4-3665-5585-a12b-bb1d508ad121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6815ae09-6f05-5b7b-9ca9-f709c3e26769" :question/math-academy-id "q-36066" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2065775ae6372e8c820b5e2f19f6f105e032dcd37db1e32e04af5bfa6a4faf9.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in [1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$ and $x\\in (0,2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/3c/3c5bc724ee29aee7bef2790012bf0e73ce1ed087134213dbad36a670fd136a36.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[1,4)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/03/03b9d70513a4ef99b39c9f05d0c0ac803f8e5611d0967015e9c1d9c0f45bd418.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c89bf3bc-912d-524b-b8c7-166e854b250f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438242} {:answer/id #uuid "c6255188-de6f-5359-b3ce-b11fa26ffa9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c89bf3bc-912d-524b-b8c7-166e854b250f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438242} :answer-field/id #uuid "35f5bf02-6bde-5643-acf0-85bec1bb3263" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c10d5b55-5751-534e-848f-312026170d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438244} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e0d146-26cc-5512-87e3-871fc6ff47b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e0d146-26cc-5512-87e3-871fc6ff47b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438245} :answer-field/id #uuid "edb61cc5-3d51-546d-9186-fa06d6294e86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af022492-4d4b-5fe8-ace0-066ff89badcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438246} {:answer/id #uuid "d1341450-0c68-5e67-bd60-bd2b0eef6a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af022492-4d4b-5fe8-ace0-066ff89badcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438246} :answer-field/id #uuid "781dd2b1-5946-5698-92e6-edc4b9e58172" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b24e31b-6e93-5c8b-93d0-5c6b5852eeb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36934" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-3,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d8/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/bc/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6ffe837-0ba9-566a-847f-01c50e5b0d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438254} {:answer/id #uuid "0c851c6e-8e6f-5ce1-85f0-794bba8508bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c851c6e-8e6f-5ce1-85f0-794bba8508bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438255} :answer-field/id #uuid "ece7019d-4e4a-54c5-8c4b-3ee796bd1176" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69b3cb09-83cc-54f2-9f3a-46d5234e0bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438256} {:answer/id #uuid "e013cbff-c909-515f-a71d-027cdb4811c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b3cb09-83cc-54f2-9f3a-46d5234e0bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438256} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bcb1241-521a-5c92-ac65-6398206509ea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1785546f-b00e-5a43-be50-0c26a6fc2ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438258} {:answer/id #uuid "1c201000-e71f-5609-9f1d-19bba5ab4630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1785546f-b00e-5a43-be50-0c26a6fc2ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438258} :answer-field/id #uuid "e28dc200-2ac1-54de-90ea-6e018bd1ba08" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "084b3fe8-adf9-5ab7-9017-b2d4d829ca62" :question/math-academy-id "q-38179" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $E$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $E$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $E$ is **not**  a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(E)=-2$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 8\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(40-42)-3(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{12}{3})+4(\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{12}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(E)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79e4e142-7005-54c1-8d51-b38fccf87ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438260} {:answer/id #uuid "54cfd4e5-c485-53e9-8b91-e2afca217595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79e4e142-7005-54c1-8d51-b38fccf87ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438260} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0815ad-f485-5e0c-8048-0318325f0ad4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f7c0c3a-e50c-57b3-b6e3-787c897947c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438262} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0b4616-bf0b-52ad-8642-7f8e6022ec10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c0b4616-bf0b-52ad-8642-7f8e6022ec10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438263} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef01e74d-81a9-5880-81c3-faa3592706db" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ce5156b-be05-52db-8fa2-508a2bebc677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438264} {:answer/id #uuid "5c652fd1-d715-5a76-8fb9-1477a177d25a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ce5156b-be05-52db-8fa2-508a2bebc677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438264} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4c6df6b-8841-5610-8b0d-3ae518f8442e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2a72ef8-dad7-5172-8868-8d2781696df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38182" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **II.** $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(Q)=-5$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(8-14)+6(5-8) \\\\  & =0-3\\cdot (-6)+6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "834b4bf2-1b3f-5d4c-b491-7c02c93b219d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438272} {:answer/id #uuid "0d78d218-e768-5739-88e2-395aa7b97bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d78d218-e768-5739-88e2-395aa7b97bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438273} :answer-field/id #uuid "3261d56f-16e4-5e60-975f-57584426806f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23eb9a8c-3df5-5681-8e74-07043805cab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438274} {:answer/id #uuid "049c70be-8905-50c7-afdd-44a53874517c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23eb9a8c-3df5-5681-8e74-07043805cab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438274} :answer-field/id #uuid "742164e8-41f0-546c-b779-b81e59044b5b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db18b8f2-ea83-5fef-a642-7bbba6480576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438276} {:answer/id #uuid "80d5c6ad-057f-53d5-b496-f302316f61f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db18b8f2-ea83-5fef-a642-7bbba6480576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438276} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fc05ecc-740b-590b-bb06-34ae388c9b15" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f729aa18-847a-50e3-929f-e0ca720e3184" :question/math-academy-id "q-38680" :question/problem "![](images/68/682105815047990048e100ea59c2652e48c0deea8c8caa422bfe3efca7d11c65.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are correct?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n- **II.** $x=-1$ is a simple root.\n- **III.** $x=2$ is a root of even multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The root $x=-1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c3d270-4f2a-53d7-8062-8d2e9cbcdce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438278} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8eef91-6406-5add-96a7-f9eabef0d91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f8eef91-6406-5add-96a7-f9eabef0d91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438279} :answer-field/id #uuid "1da65ceb-5594-5e44-bb39-79c87b94bf6f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739a4d76-6103-5d84-90a1-9822e2f320c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438280} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea74f05-534d-5d4b-9392-375d31647dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ea74f05-534d-5d4b-9392-375d31647dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438281} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a0193f-d631-5929-9c6e-41674a92b0c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4175bc45-7a87-5063-b600-76a60ad7f40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438282} {:answer/id #uuid "f897869b-bbb9-53aa-9454-68a151292859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4175bc45-7a87-5063-b600-76a60ad7f40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438282} :answer-field/id #uuid "92c5a7e5-4803-5105-b804-5b0e1a2d5217" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbe22a70-053f-5354-8d7b-dc32dacb2db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-38770" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd19717bd41b787346a96394ce3bc4e38fe690340bb73bd3d11139d41ff977e2.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=2$ is a simple root.\n\n- **II.** $x=-1$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\n- **III.** $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=2$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=-1$  has an even multiplicity because at $x=-1$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6661618c-5142-5303-9ab6-c061597132f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438284} {:answer/id #uuid "88c1c06f-e22b-5743-a5df-f566bbf4aa81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6661618c-5142-5303-9ab6-c061597132f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438284} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6acb8c1-132c-52c2-ab5b-437bf2d6f098" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2e61267-f650-507a-a46c-35c4eddb5430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438286} {:answer/id #uuid "92f87947-b439-59ca-b88e-db6ab3dd76d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92f87947-b439-59ca-b88e-db6ab3dd76d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438287} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8d6fc7d-b92b-532a-a9e3-35af311928ef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d72f815-f4b0-5fe6-85cf-34f1b56e3159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438288} {:answer/id #uuid "bc96f23f-d359-54dc-b7e6-715d86f06b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc96f23f-d359-54dc-b7e6-715d86f06b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438289} :answer-field/id #uuid "52431db6-f190-5458-b507-431d7dff764d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84c10818-73ce-58a0-a3d2-b4c129acbe6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-38779" :question/problem "![](images/73/737052513985954a32dcce369fce60f898474db846319ca31b36e3e4682b4b37.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-4$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **II.** $p(0)=3.$\n- **III.** $x=1$ is a root of odd multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-4$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-4$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=3$, which means that $p(0)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at the point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c6bb28-f335-5bbd-98ef-7c10debcd116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438308} {:answer/id #uuid "f443bd43-943d-5991-a1db-7e129b593206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f443bd43-943d-5991-a1db-7e129b593206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438309} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe78ff6-d1f1-58f5-8add-6b463affc7cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07dc0e6-51e2-5ce8-a1b4-44727450bef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438310} {:answer/id #uuid "cef77811-df7c-59ed-a36f-ed5228a3ebc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07dc0e6-51e2-5ce8-a1b4-44727450bef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438310} :answer-field/id #uuid "371815f8-f16e-5680-9ce5-31f3cff1d9be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76c420bb-1528-5dc2-9b89-925a5134c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438312} {:answer/id #uuid "f06b9547-425a-5254-b4f6-2c95fe1f7d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c420bb-1528-5dc2-9b89-925a5134c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438312} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ba6e7f7-ddb2-5a5c-9829-6eb52ab534d3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7fc84187-05b2-57ce-8e48-261250d11c80" :question/math-academy-id "q-42116" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **II.** ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $A$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since the result of ${A}^{T}-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a72f0e3-10f9-5627-abc6-e3f1fa8f8634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438314} {:answer/id #uuid "e39e9c9e-b76e-54bc-917d-488397305de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39e9c9e-b76e-54bc-917d-488397305de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438315} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07a11c2-3a82-577e-86eb-fdf2c8fb7f18" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a260fa98-0877-521e-9d9f-d5b6a870fdd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438316} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc1372a-793e-581e-ba95-60ccf10a257d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a260fa98-0877-521e-9d9f-d5b6a870fdd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438316} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4d5181e-ff19-543a-8abc-820b23948742" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ddcb0bf-22bc-580a-9f9f-9c09ea70ffbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438318} {:answer/id #uuid "b8110f84-150f-541f-b756-551b0e23ad1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ddcb0bf-22bc-580a-9f9f-9c09ea70ffbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438318} :answer-field/id #uuid "33037cbe-1756-5c5e-b354-7c66976c18f6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18223e97-17ad-509c-a688-bf8d869b747a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48040" :question/problem "![](images/59/59c02273515e87fcebb8eb1785dc2cf0c6490feda4fc9644df43b8849921eec5.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$ and we have $f(-1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, both left-hand side and right-hand side limits exist but they are not the same. Therefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function contains a break exactly at $x=-1$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8e886b-57f2-59c5-b759-e8c984922226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae70a57b-88e6-5264-9484-75fdbfb3d260" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c504c9e2-a62c-527b-a9e7-002c0a5d6492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438328} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d2fa27-53f5-5bde-85b6-c4f96e3a4c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d2fa27-53f5-5bde-85b6-c4f96e3a4c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438329} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ed00390-f87b-59cf-b29a-87e97f2baa99" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd6d307-6b90-5d32-8396-2192f0a65d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438330} {:answer/id #uuid "278fac04-a440-5c31-bf6f-e56fa749884f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bd6d307-6b90-5d32-8396-2192f0a65d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438330} :answer-field/id #uuid "4150e66a-c62a-5f54-84bd-4cbabf0439eb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96069899-bca3-51de-b64c-6e29072ea13e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48062" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9db7f2a491ae3065dbe8434a71d378c4fed8fec16c82e2fd76dcb209c786809.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)$ exists\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=1.$ The graph contains a break at $x=1.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cea1630d-9468-583c-91a2-a690bea97b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438332} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8b497a-fca1-5731-b90f-85bab2f82f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8b497a-fca1-5731-b90f-85bab2f82f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438333} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6a329d-7e8b-5bbe-84ab-3637480764d6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a5a274-c228-5909-99ce-c54b27b6c8ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438334} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f9a903-77ef-594e-8ef5-a0c888c75c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8f9a903-77ef-594e-8ef5-a0c888c75c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438335} :answer-field/id #uuid "89ad00f4-8b1c-5a88-a148-6fa4641c1832" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f597ecb7-ffec-5721-b982-5b030db741d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438336} {:answer/id #uuid "c891c5b7-7456-534a-9fcd-2f30724d3718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c891c5b7-7456-534a-9fcd-2f30724d3718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438337} :answer-field/id #uuid "87229505-3eea-5206-972c-e5c0c558ab4b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e01edc7-98f4-52fe-bf43-cb1e05ae0d4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48065" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa15192923f9fd7370818fcb6b05b24b3bb6901dfbf90dd53539d71fd0f8b0bf.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=f(2)$\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$ and $f(2)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=1=f(2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=2.$"}]}
